        "id": 1003413
      },
      "writtenOn": "2010-08-24T16:26:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I seem to have a problem with the contract itself :) When ril says that data call is disconnected (line 918 above), whats the point is asking them to disconnect again especially during power down? Its like killing a dead man :)\n\nThe direct benefit I see is that power down will be faster at least by a few ms. Also you know that modem is powered down in this case, so only thing I see in the logs is RADIO_NOT_AVAILABLE or GENERIC_FAILURE exception. If you see anything else in any of the phones that you have then it may make sense to keep this.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAA3n///zU\u003d",
      "revId": "7620c79047b8bc08afa3470bf73f15078e8c6563",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAA6H///o8\u003d",
        "filename": "telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/cdma/CdmaDataConnectionTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 928,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001401
      },
      "writtenOn": "2010-08-24T16:49:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is we don\u0027t have all the phones, we\u0027re not like other companies which control the world from end-to-end. And I agree the contract may not be good, but for a few ms once in a while its probably not worth changing at this time. Someday maybe we\u0027ll get to revisit some of these decisions.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAA6H///pE\u003d",
      "revId": "7620c79047b8bc08afa3470bf73f15078e8c6563",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
