        "id": 1003413
      },
      "writtenOn": "2010-08-24T16:26:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wink, I am bit confused about the comment. Which else are you referring to? The else in line 565 or the else in line 575 or both?\n\nThe else in line 565 is the reason for the change. In 1X we do not want to send CLEAN_UP_CONNECTION to the ril. The else in line 575 is just an optimization. I did not see the need to disconnect data call when the call is in DISCONNECTED state.\n\nIf you want to send the message in both the cases. I can send CLEAN_UP_CONNECTION with msg.arg1 set to false in both cases 1X data call and in the case where the data call is in DISCONNECTED state. It seems like a few extra redundant messages but dont see much harm in that. Please let me know your thoughts.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAA4n///OY\u003d",
      "revId": "7620c79047b8bc08afa3470bf73f15078e8c6563",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
